starch|plant-carbohydrate|NOUN|Plant carbohydrate|A carbohydrate that plants store and that occurs in foods such as rice and potatoes.|tinh bột|The cook stirred potato starch into the sauce to thicken it.|Người đầu bếp khuấy tinh bột khoai tây vào nước xốt để làm nó sánh hơn.|Usually uncountable; potato starch, corn starch. Starchy is the adjective.|-
starch|fabric-stiffener|NOUN|Fabric stiffener|A preparation containing starch that makes fabric firmer when applied to it.|hồ làm cứng vải|She sprayed starch on the collar before ironing the shirt.|Cô ấy xịt hồ lên cổ áo trước khi là chiếc áo.|Usually uncountable; spray starch, apply starch to fabric.|-
yes|affirmative-response|INTERJECTION|Affirmative response|Used to express agreement, permission or a positive answer.|vâng; có; đồng ý|Yes, you may borrow the green umbrella until tomorrow.|Vâng, bạn có thể mượn chiếc ô màu xanh lá đến ngày mai.|A response word, often followed by a comma. The Vietnamese form depends on the question and relationship between speakers.|0
considerably|substantial-degree|ADVERB|Substantial degree|By a large enough amount to make a noticeable difference.|đáng kể; nhiều|The new shelf is considerably wider than the old one.|Chiếc kệ mới rộng hơn chiếc cũ đáng kể.|Modifies comparatives or verbs: considerably larger, vary considerably.|0
handbook|practical-reference-book|NOUN|Practical reference book|A book that organizes essential information or instructions about a subject for easy consultation.|sổ tay hướng dẫn; sách tra cứu thực hành|The volunteer checked the handbook for instructions on setting up the projector.|Tình nguyện viên tra sổ tay hướng dẫn để tìm cách lắp máy chiếu.|Countable; a handbook on a subject, a staff handbook. It need not be small enough to hold in one hand.|-
lot|quantity-before-noun|DETERMINER|Large quantity before a noun|Used in a lot of or lots of to indicate a large quantity of something.|nhiều; rất nhiều|A lot of leaves collected beside the garden gate overnight.|Rất nhiều lá tụ lại bên cổng vườn qua đêm.|Use a lot of or lots of before a plural countable noun or an uncountable noun; the verb agrees with that noun.|1
lot|quantity-without-noun|PRONOUN|Large quantity without a following noun|Used in a lot or lots to refer to a large quantity already understood from context.|nhiều; rất nhiều thứ hoặc người|Some seedlings survived the frost, but a lot died.|Một số cây con sống sót qua đợt sương giá, nhưng nhiều cây đã chết.|A lot can stand without of when the noun is understood; informal. Do not write alot.|0
lot|degree-or-frequency|ADVERB|Large degree or frequent occurrence|Used in a lot to indicate a high degree or that something happens frequently.|rất nhiều; thường xuyên|My sister cycles a lot during the summer holidays.|Chị tôi đạp xe thường xuyên trong kỳ nghỉ hè.|A lot often follows the verb; a lot better strengthens a comparative. Use the two-word spelling.|2
